A||||2||Phil||Tool boxes||||1||
Z||000000||Phil||07-21-2000||10:26 PM||||Does anybody know of a source of the round tool boxes that fit into the recess in the spare tire? I believe they are called space saver tool boxes.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Philphine||07-23-2000||09:19 PM||||in case you don't find one, i've been using a canvas tool bag like the ones some military branches use. holds a pretty good amount of tools and easy to stuff in a corner of the trunk since it's pliable. surplus stores have them, $10-$20.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Carrolles||07-24-2000||08:15 AM||||I also use a bag to store my tools.  It's a typical round nylon bag that you'd use at the gym.  I wrap the tools in a towel to keep them from rattling.  Turn your spare tire upside down.  That gives more room for stuff.  I keep a gallon of coolant, a quart of oil, jumper cables, rope (to tie down a blown out tire to the luggage rack if I have a flat), and the tools.  This all fits nicely even with the sunroof stowed up front.<P>Good luck,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
